      "chunk_id": "ada595ec-d4a0-412b-9dec-047fdbf68542",
      "content": "Learning Budget\n\nEmployees receive an annual learning budget of 1,500 CAD or 1,100 USD for approved courses, books, conferences, and certifications related to their role. Manager approval is required before purchase.\n\nLearning budget requests should include the business purpose and expected outcome. The learning budget is separate from required compliance training.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-004",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "d19f25a2-9f43-402c-97f1-469af8113502",
      "content": "Procurement Thresholds\n\nPurchases below USD 2,500 may be approved by the employee's manager if the purchase is within the team's approved budget. Purchases from USD 2,500 to USD 10,000 require Finance review before a purchase order is issued.\n\nPurchases above USD 10,000 require Finance review, Legal review if a contract is involved, and department leader approval. Vendors that will process company data must complete the vendor security review before contract signature, even when the spend is below USD 10,000.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "ae3318d9-3093-40eb-bece-b2aa8ade381f",
      "content": "Related Policies\n\nTravel bookings must follow the Operations travel process. Vendor contracts must follow Legal approval rules. Software purchases must follow IT security review rules before reimbursement or procurement approval.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "2f70e93f-c560-4b48-8a79-caa4306033ef",
      "content": "Exceptions\n\nEmergency expenses are allowed when waiting for approval would create a customer, employee safety, or business-continuity risk. The employee must document the emergency and obtain manager approval within three business days.\n\nRecurring exceptions must be converted into a purchase order or department budget request. Finance does not approve repeated one-off exceptions for predictable monthly costs.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002007",
      "document_id": "FIN-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Employee",
        "Sales Representative",
        "Manager",
        "HR Admin",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "47b76ced-caf6-4234-b966-1a9cbde9e540",
      "content": "Approval Requirements\n\nEmployees must receive manager approval before changing their regular work location. A temporary change within the same country for fewer than 15 business days may be approved by the manager. Longer changes require People Operations review.\n\nManagers should consider team coverage, customer needs, time zone overlap, and data handling requirements before approving remote work.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002001",
      "document_id": "HR-003",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    }
  ],
